# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored and must never be committed, pasted into Slack/tickets,
# or shared outside the machine it runs on.
#
# This file is only for LOCAL development. A cloud routine or CI job should
# inject these as environment variables / secrets instead — real environment
# variables take precedence over this file, so no .env need exist there.
#
# Format: plain KEY=value, no `export` prefix, no surrounding quotes.
# Use --env-file to point at a file other than .env.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED for any real (non-mock) run.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
BUBBLE_API_TOKEN=your-bubble-api-token-here

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Which Bubble environment this deployment targets. Keeping it here rather
# than in config.json means the production URL never has to be committed to
# the repo — a routine targeting production just sets this variable.
#
# Must be https:// — the API token is sent as a Bearer header, and the script
# refuses plaintext HTTP.
#
# Ignored when --use-test-version is passed: that flag always wins, so an
# explicit request for staging can't be redirected to production by a value
# left in here. Not needed for --mock runs at all.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BUBBLE_BASE_URL=https://app.quietlist.com.au/api/1.1/obj

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL. Enables uploading generated PDFs to Drive (see README.md's
# "Uploading PDFs to Drive" section for the one-time service-account setup).
#
# The RAW JSON CONTENT of a Google Cloud service account key — not a file
# path. That service account must be shared (Editor) on the Drive folder
# given by drive_reports_folder_id in config.json.
#
# Left unset: generate_report.py behaves exactly as before (PDFs only in
# ./reports), and run_scheduled_report.py logs a clear skip message instead
# of failing. Nothing here is required for --mock or --use-test-version runs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON={"type":"service_account","project_id":"...","private_key":"...","client_email":"...", ...}
